<title>UK: EMI denies merger talks with MCA. [CORRECTED 23:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>EMI denies merger talks with MCA. [CORRECTED 23:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline to read MCA rather than MCI.)</p>
<p>Music publisher EMI on Sunday denied a newspaper report that it has approached Seagram Co Ltd about merging all or part of its business with the latter's MCA Music division.</p>
<p>&quot;This is complete rubbish. There are not any conversations going on,&quot; said an EMI spokesman.</p>
<p>The Independent on Sunday said talks were going on between the two companies despite an initial frosty reception from Seagram.</p>
<p>Stock market talk about a possible merger has driven EMI shares higher in recent weeks.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
